=== p2-windows · W7 · page:vehicle-systems/Maintenance (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:vehicle-systems/Maintenance   kind=page   web route=/maintenance
Web source  : web/src/features/vehicle-systems/pages/MaintenancePage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/MaintenancePage/{MaintenancePage.Model.cs,
              MaintenancePage.Source.cs, MaintenancePage.ViewModel.cs, MaintenancePage.cs}
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  VehicleCostPage / ApiLogsPage / DiagnosticPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "MaintenancePage.xaml + MaintenancePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/VehicleSystems" is mapped onto these
  real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Maintenance", already
  in RouteTable.cs L270 -> /maintenance, group VehicleSystems) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the web page runs two raw queries — request<MaintenanceItem[]>('/maintenance') and
  request<ServiceRecord[]>('/maintenance/records'). Both operations exist in the generated OpenAPI contract client
  (Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs): get_api_v1_maintenance (GET /maintenance/) and get_api_v1_maintenance_records
  (GET /maintenance/records), each returning JsonElement with no parameters/body. The manifest's "no API data sources"
  note reflects the generator not detecting the raw request<>() calls; the surface nonetheless binds both operations
  through an injected IMaintenanceFeed. The default EmptyMaintenanceFeed resolves the empty state; the
  generated-client-backed MaintenanceClientFeed (MaintenancePage.Source.cs) issues both operations and combines them
  into a MaintenanceSnapshot, asserted via the FakeApiClient (ClientFeed_sends_both_maintenance_operations). No HTTP
  touches the view; a non-success response surfaces as ApiException and the view-model folds it into the failure
  banner (web anyError), asserted by ViewModel_api_exception_is_the_error_state. Tolerant parsers accept both a bare
  JSON array and the platform {data:[…]} envelope (Items_parse_from_a_bare_array / Records_parse_from_a_data_envelope).
- The web page renders its states INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent
  regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; failure -> TsAlertBanner(Danger)
  above the content (web anyError AlertBanner); empty -> the four summary stat cards + panels still render while the
  item grid shows a TsEmptyState; success -> the full body. Never a blank region. The error banner sits ABOVE the
  content exactly as the web composes it (ShowError && ShowContent both true).
- Client-side category filter (web categoryFilter / setCategoryFilter) and sort (web sortBy / setSortBy /
  SORT_OPTIONS) are modelled on the view-model and re-project WITHOUT re-fetching
  (ViewModel_set_category_filters_without_refetching / ViewModel_set_sort_reprojects_without_refetching). The
  category options are derived from the loaded items (web categories memo) and capitalized; the four sort keys are
  static (status/name/due_date/category).
- All per-item logic is a faithful port of the web helpers: computeProgress (mile interval -> month interval ->
  due-mileage ratio, clamped 0..100), statusFromPct (>=90 overdue / >=70 soon / else good), derivedStatus
  (completed stays completed), STATUS_BADGE_MAP, STATUS_SORT_ORDER, the cost-stats span-years calculation
  (single record -> total as annual+avg; >=2 dated records -> total / max(span,0.1)), and the projections build
  (non-completed interval items, overdue first then by miles remaining, slice 8). Asserted by the ComputeProgress_*,
  Item_card_*, Cost_*, Projections_* tests.
- SI / display formatting (ADR-005): counts via NumberFormatting.Format (web fmtNumber, 0 dp); currency via "$" +
  NumberFormatting (web formatCurrency, 0 dp on the cost cards, 2 dp on the records cost cell, web Currency); dates
  via DateTimeFormatting Date / Full variants (web formatDate / formatDateTime). Pinned by FormatCount_matches_web /
  FormatCurrency_matches_web theories.
- The web AIPredictiveMaintenance card (web/src/components/ai/AIPredictiveMaintenance) is an opt-in shared component
  that returns null when ai_mode='off' or the predictive-maintenance toggle is off; it is NOT one of the 11 manifest
  panels (its own W3 component parity unit owns it). The deterministic reminders/summary above remain the canonical
  baseline exactly as the web comment states, so the surface is at panel parity without it. The header VehicleSelect
  is shell-level global vehicle chrome (the maintenance endpoints are vehicle-agnostic in the generated contract,
  taking no vehicle_id param) and is not a manifest panel; the page header reproduces the web title + subtitle.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves through the ILocalizer facade using the EXACT web key names (the web
  uses the English string as the key, e.g. t('Total Items'), plus the dotted t('error.loadFailed')). 19 missing
  manifest keys + 3 supporting keys (Category, Due Date sort labels, the "general" category fallback) were added to
  Strings/en/Resources.resw as translation.<webKey> (the other 11 manifest keys — Completed, Cost, Date, Description,
  Due, Maintenance, Mileage, Overdue, Provider, error.loadFailed, mi — already existed). The ar/he catalogs lag en by
  design; the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view is
  excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). A self-contained internal JsonReadHelpers (Str/Long/Double) lives in the
  MaintenancePage.Model.cs vehicle-systems namespace (mirrors the DBHealthPage precedent of a per-namespace copy).
- Pre-existing build break repaired (NOT my surface, but it blocks the shared TeslaSync.App Release build the gate
  requires): a prior W7 commit (3f642976f "MQTTInspectorPage at web parity") left two CA1822 errors latent in
  feature-views/MQTTInspectorPage/MQTTInspectorPage.cs (BuildConnectionContent / BuildThroughputContent do not access
  instance data). They only surface on a clean Release rebuild; the canonical fix (mark both `private static`) was
  applied so the solution builds 0/0. My own MaintenancePage files compiled clean on the first app-project build (the
  only two errors reported were the MQTTInspectorPage pair).

